      "problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251131/assets/1349a7c34fd6656464dbf0d86cbc41a57e3a72971ee5351a9892808ed22e19bb.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251131/assets/157db264f983882569643be7539011d27673032557e47bbad722d8917dd4d620.svg)\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$",
